Title: NICK AND ME
Credit: adapted from the book
Author: short-film pre-production draft

[[Schema note: VO is narrator; given name withheld until final scene.]]

FADE IN:

== S01 KIRK STREET APARTMENT - DAY/NIGHT MONTAGE ==

A fifth-floor walk-up. Brick. Groceries. A LARGE MAN (NICK) carries too many bags like a strongman contest. YOUNGER BROTHER follows with the rest.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Not the book. My real Big Brother. Nick.

Nick's face: scars on chin and over left eyebrow; hair uncombed; the room notices him even here.

MA in her chair, game show light on tired eyes. Pill bottles in a straight line on the kitchen counter.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I lived with him and Ma after dad took off when I was about eight. Milwaukee. Kirk Street.

== S02 PIZZA PLACE SIDEWALK - DAY ==

Younger Brother bikes up, walks to the door. A young woman (SIONNA) trips on cement, brushes his shoulder. Short brown hair. Black V-neck. Fish-symbol necklace. Light blue eyes.

They steady. A look too long.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Are you okay—yes—I work here—what is your name—

She answers. The name sits strange in the air: Sionna.

She declines pizza, offers coffee instead, leaves a number. Walks away, glances back over her shoulder.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
It was like I knew her. Intense. Like tides coming in and I didn't want to move my feet.

== S03 LIBRARY - NIGHT ==

Cold street. Library lights. Wood floors. Chain-hung lamps. Desk. A temporary paper card.

Stacks. Classic literature. A hand takes WUTHERING HEIGHTS.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Who needed school when you could get the same thing free?

== S04 JAVA HUT - DAY ==

College backpacks. Sionna at a small back table. Green hooded top. Watery blue eyes.

They talk books. Ghosts. Moors. Love that never changes.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
She said a love that never changes will destroy you. It reminded me of Nick—strong, unwavering. I wondered if it would destroy him too.

Something in him wakes.

== S05 KIRK APARTMENT - DAY ==

Ma hunts pain pills already lined on the counter. Glassy empty eyes.

MA
Did we go to church today? Did you see Mrs. Canasta there?

We haven't, not for years. He steadies her. Later: Nick angry—missed doctor's appointment—priorities—a girl.

Door slam.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
God, sometimes I really hate Nick inside. I would never tell anybody that.

== S06 JOE'S BAR AND GRILL - NIGHT ==

Smoke. Pool. Rock music. Nick parts the crowd. Ex-girlfriend Lindsey with a dark-haired man. Nick's face goes red-fire.

Younger Brother steps between.

Noise drops toward the fist. Slow. Heartbeat.

Bouncers. Chaos. Younger Brother RUNS—street, cold air—until lungs burn.

== S07 SIONNA'S DUPLEX - NIGHT ==

He collapses into her calm. Head in her lap.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
The first time I met you I felt like I had finally come home.

TIME CUT:

Later months. School. Care. Distance from Nick.

Then: Nick at her door. Cold. Rage. He crowds her to the hallway wall. Switchblade opens.

Front door THUNKS open. Younger Brother. Struggle. Blade hits. Red. She sinks. Nick wipes the knife on her shirt and flees into dark.

Hands on wound. Sirens.

== S08 POLICE / HOSPITAL / EMPTY APT - NIGHT ==

Stone station. An officer's mouth moves.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Broadside—Werner and Lowe—Nick serious—Ma passed away at the scene.

ICU glass: Nick's wild hair above white bedding, tubes. Younger Brother turns away.

Empty apartment. Ma's chair. Afghan. He breaks—rage at the brother who drove drunk from church.

== S09 SEATTLE - YEARS LATER ==

Grey blanket sky. Rain hoods. A pizza storefront: TONY'S BOY'S PIZZA. Adult Narrator walks like a local.

Yoga candles. Cat Bozo. A dream-sage and a dirty pizza box that vanishes when judgment drops.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Holding resentment kept me in my own prison. I had to see Nick.

Laptop. Flight to Milwaukee.

== S10 GREEN BAY CORRECTIONAL - DAY ==

Locks. Plexiglass. Phones. NICK opposite—thinner, greying, old.

They stare.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
You're an asshole that killed my mother... held me down... tried to kill the love of my life.

Breath.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And this is the most important bit. I forgive you. It sets me free.

Nick's tears hit the grey counter. Pride flickers when he hears of the Seattle chain.

Guard: time.

Yellow receiver hung up. Adult Narrator walks out lighter.

AIRPORT QUEUE - BOARDING PASS

A whisper to himself—first full name:

NARRATOR (V.O.)
That's me. President Peter Olson.

This has been Nick and me.

FADE OUT.

END.
